This    project explored Automated Essay Scoring (AES) for predicting human assigned scores on essays. Three (3) modelling approaches were developed and compared; a classical TF-IDF with ridge regression model, a neural BiGRU with attention, and a fine-tuned DistilBERT transformer model. Performance was evaluated using Quadratic Weighted Kappa as the main metric, together with MAE, RMSE, and Spearman correlation. The results show that the classical feature-based model achieved the best performance on the dataset.  
